## 🧬 2. Domain Entities & Patterns

The Domain project holds the core blueprints. All custom entities must inherit from foundational base classes to ensure consistency, specifically around ID generation and auditing.

### **Base Classes**
*   [BaseEntity](file:///d:/Projects/Saay/SaayAI/Crm8-sql/Crm/src/Crm.Domain/Common/BaseEntity.cs#6-19): Provides a standard `long Id` and a `NotMapped` list for `DomainEvents` (useful for publishing domain-driven events later).
*   [AuditableEntity](file:///d:/Projects/Saay/SaayAI/Crm8-sql/Crm/src/Crm.Domain/Common/AuditableEntity.cs#3-10): Inherits from [BaseEntity](file:///d:/Projects/Saay/SaayAI/Crm8-sql/Crm/src/Crm.Domain/Common/BaseEntity.cs#6-19) and adds `CreatedOn`, `CreatedById`, `ModifiedOn`, and `ModifiedById`.

### **Entity Creation Standard:**
**Rule:** When creating a new entity, inherit from [AuditableEntity](file:///d:/Projects/Saay/SaayAI/Crm8-sql/Crm/src/Crm.Domain/Common/AuditableEntity.cs#3-10). 
```csharp
[Auditable] // Optional metadata attribute
public class Customer : AuditableEntity
{
    [Required]
    [MaxLength(200)]
    public string Name { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
```

*Note on Users:* The [User](file:///d:/Projects/Saay/SaayAI/Crm8-sql/Crm/src/Crm.Domain/Entities/User.cs#9-53) class inherits from `IdentityUser<long>`, but manually replicates the `IAuditableEntity` properties since C# lacks multiple inheritance.

