## 🛡️ 4. Middlewares & Cross-Cutting Concerns

### **Global Exception Handling**
Do not use `try/catch` blocks in controllers or handlers for standard flow.
The [ExceptionHandlingMiddleware](file:///d:/Projects/Saay/SaayAI/Crm8-sql/Crm/src/Crm.Api/Middleware/ExceptionHandlingMiddleware.cs#18-23) intercepts everything:
*   [ValidationException](file:///d:/Projects/Saay/SaayAI/Crm8-sql/Crm/src/Crm.Api/Middleware/ExceptionHandlingMiddleware.cs#57-69) (from FluentValidation) -> Translated to standard HTTP 400 with a custom `ApiBadRequestResponse`.
*   [NotFoundException](file:///d:/Projects/Saay/SaayAI/Crm8-sql/Crm/src/Crm.Api/Middleware/ExceptionHandlingMiddleware.cs#70-82) -> Translated to HTTP 404.
*   `Unhandled Exceptions` -> Translated to HTTP 500, preventing stack traces from leaking to clients in production.

